EXT. MUNICIPAL POOL - TEN-METER DIVING TOWER - NIGHT

Chain-link fence. Empty bleachers. The water is black, lit only by one emergency lamp. Three teens climb the concrete tower.

IZZY PAREDES, 16, steps onto the platform first. Hoodie, bare feet, a bag of stolen fireworks.

WYATT BRODERICK, 17, follows, taller, breathing hard from the stairs.

SOLENNE ADEYEMI-CHANG, 16, brings up the rear with her phone light off. She keeps one hand on the rail.

IZZY
Look at that. Whole town.

WYATT
It's a parking lot and a Taco Bell.

IZZY
It's our parking lot.

SOLENNE
Can we just go back down?

IZZY
You said you wanted to see it.

SOLENNE
From the bottom.

Wyatt laughs. Solenne glares.

WYATT
You jumped from the five last summer.

SOLENNE
I fell from the five.

Izzy digs in the bag. Pulls out a firework. Holds it up like a trophy.

IZZY
Tonight we send Mr. Hendricks off.

WYATT
He's not dead, Izzy. He retired.

IZZY
Same thing. Teachers don't get better.

She flicks a lighter. Nothing. Again. Nothing.

WYATT
Give it.

IZZY
No.

WYATT
You'll blow your hand off.

IZZY
You'll blow your hand off.

They tussle. The firework drops. Rolls. Solenne dives and catches it with both hands.

SOLENNE
Stop it! Both of you!

They freeze. Wyatt's hand still on Izzy's sleeve.

Quiet. Wind on the water. Far below, a car passes.

WYATT
(softer)
Sorry.

IZZY
Yeah.

They let go. Izzy sits on the edge, legs over. Wyatt sits beside her. Solenne stays upright.

SOLENNE
Is it weird that I'm going to miss this place?

WYATT
It's a pool.

SOLENNE
It's where we learned to swim.

IZZY
I learned to swim in a bathtub.

WYATT
That's not swimming. That's drowning slowly.

Izzy shoves him. He shoves back. They both nearly tip. Solenne yanks both by the hoods.

SOLENNE
Okay! No dying tonight. We have prom.

IZZY
Prom is stupid.

SOLENNE
Prom is the last thing before everything.

Silence. Izzy picks at the platform's grit.

IZZY
My mom's moving us to Tucson.

WYATT
When?

IZZY
August.

WYATT
You didn't tell us.

IZZY
I'm telling you now.

Solenne sits. All three in a row. Legs dangling.

SOLENNE
We could jump.

WYATT
We could.

IZZY
All three?

SOLENNE
All three.

They stand. Hold hands. Breathe.

WYATT
On three.

IZZY
On one. Three is a trap.

SOLENNE
One!

They leap together, screaming, into the black.

SPLASH. Then laughter. Echoing.

Overhead, a floodlight clicks on. A flashlight beam sweeps the water.

A whistle shrieks from the fence line.

The three scramble out, shrieking, dripping, stumbling over each other, laughing so hard they can barely climb the fence.
